  "Poet, editor and magazine writer; the most popular magazine writer in America in the 1840s and the inventor of the American society column.",
  "Born in Portland, Maine, on 20 January 1806; he travelled in Europe as a foreign correspondent, edited the American Monthly Magazine and the New York Mirror, and made his fortune with the Home Journal from 1846. His Sketches (1835), Letters from Under a Bridge (1840) and Out-Doors at Idlewild (1855) were widely read. He died at Idlewild, his estate on the Hudson, on 20 January 1867.",
