  "Tuckerman wrote the finest American sonnet sequence of the nineteenth century and was the most original nature poet of his generation: his Poems of 1860, largely ignored in his lifetime, were rediscovered in the twentieth century as a central text of American poetry, and his influence runs through Yvor Winters, Robert Frost and the American formal lyric.",
