  "Born Celia Laighton in Portsmouth, New Hampshire, on 29 June 1835; she grew up on White Island and then Appledore in the Isles of Shoals, where her father kept the lighthouse and later a hotel. Poems (1872), Among the Isles of Shoals (1873), Drift-Weed (1878) and An Island Garden (1894) followed. She died at the Isles of Shoals on 26 August 1894.",
